-- Thue's lemma by pigeonhole: for 0 < p and m with m² > p and m ≤ p, every
-- a has a nonzero pair (x, y) of integers of absolute value below m with
-- a x ≡ y modulo p; with the least such m, and in a natural form with a
-- positive x.
-- Part of Cumulus, the Grace17 mathematics library.
